WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:17,710
Have you heard of the SIGNATERA test personalized test that detects your cancer

00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:31,470
circulating tumor, D&A, used to detect relapse, measure, treatment for efficacy and it's

00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:38,190
covered by insurance for a medium to late-stage cancer, solid tumor cancers?

00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:47,790
So if you could do a test like this that is going to measure a circulating tumor, D&A,

00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:54,750
that is covered by insurance and by all means go ahead and do it. It is a blood test and it's not

00:00:54,750 --> 00:01:02,350
going to be invasive. But if you have to pay out a pocket, you're spending $2,000 for it.

00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:10,110
It's not giving you quantitative data that is going to be able to measure, you know, it's just

00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:18,510
that whether it's going to go up or down, so there's positives and negatives to this test. But

00:01:19,390 --> 00:01:24,910
that was the beauty of the IVG test. When we had that, it gave you more quantitative numbers so

00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:30,830
that you could see if your cancer is getting worse or better. This will tell you if your cancer is

00:01:30,910 --> 00:01:39,230
active but it doesn't tell you how active it doesn't give you that same data, but it could be helpful.

00:01:40,590 --> 00:01:48,670
It's not a perfect test but you have to remember, no test is a perfect test. So

00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:57,630
it's just it does, the last time I looked at it, maybe they changed their prices,

00:01:58,190 --> 00:02:02,270
it was a couple of thousand dollars for the test. So if the insurance covers it, then that's great.

00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:07,710
